# Raw per-run artifacts under raw/<device>/... ARE committed (they back every
# RESULTS.md table):
#   runN.log        — sanitized by run.sh at capture time to ONLY the
#                     perf/marker lines stats.py parses (frust-perf /
#                     flutter-perf / bench-scenario-*). Full-device logcat
#                     never persists.
#   *.pss_*.txt     — `dumpsys meminfo <our bench pkg>` snapshots (S7 memory
#                     axis); scoped to our own app's process only.
#   coldstart.txt   — S7 only: `am start -W` output for our own bench package
#                     (intent, LaunchState, TotalTime/WaitTime), written by
#                     matrix.sh's post-matrix external cold-start loop.
#   cpuinfo.txt     — S7 only: `dumpsys cpuinfo` lines grep-filtered to our
#                     own bench package + the TOTAL line, sampled every 30s
#                     during the S7 blocks by matrix.sh.
#   *.sysmon.txt    — iOS S7 only: the bench pid's Instruments `sysmon-process`
#                     rows (`t_s= cpu_pct= cpu_ns= footprint_bytes= rss_bytes=`)
#                     over the tail of every other kept run, written by run.sh
#                     --sysmon via sysmon_export.py; the all-process trace and
#                     XML it comes from never persist.
#   coldstart.txt (iOS) — matrix.sh's FrontBoard cold-start loop: per launch a
#                     `== launch N <ts> (ios: FrontBoard bootstrap -> scene
#                     content ready)` header, the two SpringBoard(FrontBoard)
#                     anchor lines naming only our bundle id, and the derived
#                     `TotalTime: <ms>`; the device syslog capture it is cut
#                     from never persists.
#   stats.txt       — the run.sh stdout tail from its `-- stats.py` banner
#                     onward (the stats.py p50=/p95=/frames:/missed_* table
#                     for that scenario's kept runs); whitelist-checked
#                     line-by-line the same way as runN.log, by
#                     ab_matrix.sh's self_check_raw_dir.
# Pre-commit verification (run all three by hand — one line per committed
# artifact class above; the stats.txt expression is ab_matrix.sh's
# STATS_WHITELIST_RE verbatim, keep the two identical):
#   grep -rlvE 'frust-perf|flutter-perf|bench-scenario|^[[:space:]]*$' raw/ --include='*.log'   (expect no output)
#   scan *.pss_*.txt for any package identifier other than it.f0x.*bench     (expect none)
#   every *.sysmon.txt line matches matrix.sh's SYSMON_WHITELIST_RE and every coldstart.txt
#     line matches its COLDSTART_WHITELIST_RE (stage_raw.sh carries both verbatim; run it over
#     a staged tree, or grep -rlvE with the expression)                      (expect no output)
#   grep -rlvE '^-- stats\.py( --dclass)? \(discarding first [0-9]+ runs?, per protocol convention\) --$|^== [A-Za-z0-9_. ()-]+ ==$|^frames: [0-9]+ total, [0-9]+ active, [0-9]+ skipped$|^p50=[0-9.]+ms[[:space:]]+p95=[0-9.]+ms[[:space:]]+p99=[0-9.]+ms[[:space:]]+worst=[0-9.]+ms$|^missed_60hz=[0-9]+ \(budget [0-9.]+ms\)[[:space:]]+missed_120hz=[0-9]+ \(budget [0-9.]+ms\)$|^[[:space:]]*$' raw/ --include='stats.txt'   (expect no output)
# Transient capture scratch (pre-sanitize) — never committed:
*.unfiltered
*.console.txt
*.container.txt
